WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.698 --> 00:00:02.197
- [Narrator] Is this a sandwich?

00:00:02.197 --> 00:00:03.855
How about this?

00:00:03.855 --> 00:00:05.488
Or this?

00:00:05.488 --> 00:00:08.155
The answer is, well, it depends.

00:00:11.579 --> 00:00:13.389
- [Neal] It's actually surprisingly

00:00:13.389 --> 00:00:16.299
complicated jurisdiction scheme.

00:00:16.299 --> 00:00:18.258
- [Narrator] That's Neal
Fortin, he's a professor

00:00:18.258 --> 00:00:22.187
of food law, he wrote the
book on it, literally.

00:00:22.187 --> 00:00:23.848
Just what a sandwich is

00:00:23.848 --> 00:00:26.240
is actually defined by the government.

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:29.805
Federally, it's the USDA and the FDA.

00:00:29.805 --> 00:00:32.558
Defining something
matters because it changes

00:00:32.558 --> 00:00:35.019
how it's inspected and regulated.

00:00:35.019 --> 00:00:38.480
- [Neal] The hot dog is regulated by USDA,

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:42.656
but a hot dog on a bun
is regulated by FDA.

00:00:42.656 --> 00:00:46.299
A sandwich doesn't have actually
a strict legal definition,

00:00:46.299 --> 00:00:48.549
it's more of the common term.

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:51.560
- [Narrator] That can lead
to some heated arguments

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:54.789
by sandwich purists,
according to the USDA,

00:00:54.789 --> 00:00:56.920
the hot dog is not a sandwich,

00:00:56.920 --> 00:00:58.548
but the dictionary says it is,

00:00:58.548 --> 00:01:01.109
and so does the state of New York.

00:01:01.109 --> 00:01:03.548
New York is pretty inclusive
on the sandwich question.

00:01:03.548 --> 00:01:06.448
- Hi, I'm David Greco,
this is Mike's Deli,

00:01:06.448 --> 00:01:08.509
in the real Little Italy of the Bronx.

00:01:08.509 --> 00:01:11.429
Our list of sandwiches is
at least 50 sandwiches,

00:01:11.429 --> 00:01:13.528
we have The Bronx Tale, The Michelangelo,

00:01:13.528 --> 00:01:17.248
The Sophia Loren, The Raging
Bull, The Yankee Big Boy.

00:01:17.248 --> 00:01:20.440
Come on, I'll make you one special.

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:23.280
That's a New York sandwich.

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:24.819
- [Narrator] According to
the state's Department of

00:01:24.819 --> 00:01:27.408
Taxation and Finance,
not only is a hot dog

00:01:27.408 --> 00:01:29.768
a sandwich, but so is a burrito.

00:01:29.768 --> 00:01:31.848
That's because a burrito counts as a wrap,

00:01:31.848 --> 00:01:35.080
which in New York is a sandwich.

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:36.807
Okay, so what about this?

00:01:36.807 --> 00:01:39.640
It looks and acts like a sandwich.

00:01:40.559 --> 00:01:42.691
- [Neal] Is an ice cream
sandwich a sandwich?

00:01:42.691 --> 00:01:43.968
I would say that ice cream sandwich

00:01:43.968 --> 00:01:47.324
is a fanciful name
rather than an actual use

00:01:47.324 --> 00:01:49.534
of the word sandwich
in a traditional sense.

00:01:49.534 --> 00:01:52.094
- [Narrator] Fanciful
name, delicious sandwich.

00:01:52.094 --> 00:01:56.033
The USDA disagrees, but what do they know?

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:58.301
However a sandwich is
defined, we know that they're

00:01:58.301 --> 00:02:00.342
all kinds of delicious.

00:02:00.342 --> 00:02:02.334
- [Neal] Food law is, it's both simpler

00:02:02.334 --> 00:02:06.073
and much more complicated
than it looks on the surface.

00:02:06.073 --> 00:02:08.156
- [Narrator] Thanks Neal.

